### Step 3: Implement `src/moshier/moon.rs`

All computation code. Key structures and functions:

**MeanElements struct** — returned by `mean_elements()`, no TLS state:
```rust
pub struct MeanElements {
    pub m: f64,     // solar anomaly l' (arcsec)
    pub nf: f64,    // F (arcsec)
    pub mp: f64,    // lunar anomaly l (arcsec)
    pub d: f64,     // elongation (arcsec)
    pub swelp: f64, // mean lunar longitude L (arcsec)
}

pub fn mean_elements(t: f64) -> MeanElements {
    let t2 = t * t;
    let frac_t = t % 1.0;
    // M: 9th-degree Laskar poly (coefficients in c-ref-moshier.md)
    let m = mods3600(129600000.0 * frac_t - 3418.961646 * t + 1287104.76154)
        + /* Laskar 9th-degree poly */ * t2;
    // NF: mods3600(...) + ((Z[2]*T + Z[1])*T + Z[0]) * T²
    // MP: mods3600(...) + ((Z[5]*T + Z[4])*T + Z[3]) * T²
    // D:  mods3600(...) + ((Z[8]*T + Z[7])*T + Z[6]) * T²
    // SWELP: mods3600(...) + ((Z[11]*T + Z[10])*T + Z[9]) * T²
    MeanElements { m, nf, mp, d, swelp }
}
```

**PlanetaryElements** — from `mean_elements_pl()`:
```rust
struct PlanetaryElements { ve: f64, ea: f64, ma: f64, ju: f64, sa: f64 }

fn mean_elements_pl(t: f64, t2: f64) -> PlanetaryElements {
    // Ve: mods3600(210664136.4335482*T + 655127.283046) + 9th-degree secular poly * T²
    // Ea: mods3600(129597742.26669231*T + 361679.214649) + 9th-degree secular poly * T²
    // Ma: mods3600(68905077.59284*T + 1279559.78866) + quadratic
    // Ju: mods3600(10925660.428608*T + 123665.342120) + quadratic
    // Sa: mods3600(4399609.65932*T + 180278.89694) + cubic
}
```

**MoonState** — stack-local struct replacing C TLS globals:
```rust
struct MoonState {
    t: f64, t2: f64, t4: f64,
    ve: f64, ea: f64, ma: f64, ju: f64, sa: f64,
    l: f64, l1: f64, l2: f64, l3: f64, l4: f64,
    b: f64,
    moonpol: [f64; 3],
    ss: [[f64; 8]; 5],
    cc: [[f64; 8]; 5],
}
```

**chewm** — harmonic table evaluator:
```rust
fn chewm(table: &[i16], nlines: usize, nangles: usize, typflg: u8,
         ans: &mut [f64; 3], ss: &[[f64; 8]; 5], cc: &[[f64; 8]; 5]) {
    // For each row: build combined sin/cos from nangles columns,
    // then dispatch on typflg:
    //   1 → lon(×10000 packed) + rad(×10000 packed, skip if k==0)
    //   2 → small lon + small rad
    //   3 → lat(×10000 packed)
    //   4 → small lat
}
```

**sscc** — sin/cos lookup for 5×8 grid (same algorithm as planet sscc, different array dims):
```rust
fn sscc(k: usize, arg: f64, n: usize,
        ss: &mut [[f64; 8]; 5], cc: &mut [[f64; 8]; 5]) {
    // Recurrence: ss[k][i] = sin((i+1)*arg), cc[k][i] = cos((i+1)*arg)
}
```

**moon1–4 and moshmoon2**:
```rust
fn moon1(state: &mut MoonState, mean: &MeanElements) {
    // Zero ss/cc, call sscc for D(6), M(4), MP(4), NF(4)
    // Phase A: chewm(LRT2, BT2), planetary perturbations via z[12..24], scale T²
    // Phase B: chewm(BT, LRT), more perturbations, scale T¹
    // NOTE: individual perturbation amplitudes extracted by reader agent from swemmoon.c
}
fn moon2(state: &mut MoonState, mean: &MeanElements) {
    // ~28 longitude + ~8 latitude T^0 planetary perturbation terms
    // Hard-coded sin/cos of Ve, Ea, Ma, Ju, Sa, SWELP, NF, D, MP combinations
}
fn moon3(state: &mut MoonState, mean: &MeanElements) {
    // chewm(LR, 118, 4, 1, ...) — main longitude + radius
    // chewm(MB, 77, 4, 3, ...)  — main latitude
    // Assemble: moonpol[0] = SWELP + l + Horner(l1..l4,T)*1e-5 + 1e-4*moonpol[0]
    //           moonpol[1] = 1e-4*moonpol[1] + B
    //           moonpol[2] = 1e-4*moonpol[2] + 385000.52899
}
fn moon4(state: &mut MoonState) {
    // moonpol[2] /= AUNIT/1000  (km → AU)
    // moonpol[0] = STR * mods3600(moonpol[0])  (arcsec → rad)
    // moonpol[1] = STR * moonpol[1]  (arcsec → rad)
}

pub fn moshmoon2(jd: f64) -> [f64; 3] {
    let t = (jd - J2000) / 36525.0;
    let t2 = t * t;
    let mean = mean_elements(t);
    let pl = mean_elements_pl(t, t2);
    let mut state = MoonState { t, t2, t4: t2*t2, /* pl fields, zeroed accumulators */ };
    moon1(&mut state, &mean);
    moon2(&mut state, &mean);
    moon3(&mut state, &mean);
    moon4(&mut state);
    state.moonpol
}
```

